Usage: hostname [OPTION]...

Print or set system name.

Print the name of the current host.

Note: This implementation only supports printing hostname.
Setting hostname is not implemented on Windows.

OPTIONS:
  -b, --boot              set default hostname if none available
  -i, --ip-address        addresses for the hostname
  -I, --all-ip-addresses  all addresses for the hostname
  -s, --short             short host name
  -f, --fqdn              long host name (FQDN)
  -a, --alias             host alias names (not supported on Windows)
  -A, --all-fqdns         all FQDNs of the host (not supported on Windows)
  -d, --domain            DNS domain name
  -F, --file ARG          read host name or NIS domain name from FILE
  -y, --yp                NIS/YP domain name (not supported on Windows)
  -n, --node              network node hostname (not supported on Windows)
      --help              display this help and exit
  -V, --version           output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
